e there  but they shouldn't be debated and the  military shouldn't be held hostage  uh with the ndaa so the president didn't  think it was the right bill to sign at  this time  he wants a strong defense he's just  submitted a 355-ship  navy shipbuilding plan that's terrific  and is paid for for many many years  uh in part because we're drawing down  and ending and wrapping up some of these  forever wars  uh so he's got a great record on defense  he's proud of it he wants a clean bill  to come back from  from the congress as soon as possible  one that he can sign  yeah and listen nobody will cheer him on  more than myself in terms of bringing  our troops home  from these endless wars uh we all we we  ought to celebrate bringing our troops  home it's amazing to me how many people  just want them to stay there in  perpetuity i think the president  is listening to the american people and  wants to bring those troops home and  needs the flexibility as the president  to do so  uh i gotta end though on china uh donald  trump has done more  from my vantage point to push back and  highlight china and  and look at what they're doing on so  many fronts  walk us through what the president's  been able to do in china i've only got  about 40 seconds  i'll be quick they hollowed out our  manufacturing by stealing our  intellectual property and and  subsidizing their their  state-owned enterprises and and buying  our our manufacturing facilities and  moving them lock stock and barrel to  china the president put on tariffs and  stop  that got a great phase one trade deal  they've extinguished freedom in hong  kong and the president's made him pay a  price for that  uh they're they're engaged in in  terrible activities in sinjar with the  uyghurs and  and destroying religious freedom they've  attacked our friends in india on the  border they've taken over the entire  south china sea and claimed that sarah's  like it's a some sort of domestic lake  like a lake tahoe  and we've stood u